# Android Paywall — Diagnostic & Production Checklist

## 🔴 Root Cause Analysis

Your symptoms (money deducted → transaction not in RevenueCat → not recognized as pro → "already subscribed" error) point to **Google Play processing the purchase natively, but RevenueCat never receiving/validating it**. This is almost certainly a **server-side credential issue** — RevenueCat can't talk to Google Play to verify the purchase.

Here's every issue I found, ranked by severity:

---

## Issue #1 (CRITICAL): RevenueCat Cannot Validate Google Play Purchases

**This is your main problem.** For RevenueCat to receive Android transactions, you need to configure a **Google Play Service Account** in the RevenueCat dashboard. Without this, Google Play processes the purchase directly but RevenueCat never knows about it.

### What happens without it:
1. User taps Subscribe → Google Play payment sheet appears → money is charged ✅
2. `Purchases.purchasePackage()` returns customer info, BUT RevenueCat backend can't verify the purchase token with Google → entitlement is **not** granted ❌
3. RevenueCat dashboard shows no transaction ❌
4. Google Play remembers the subscription → "already subscribed" error on retry ✅

### Fix (RevenueCat Dashboard):
1. Go to [RevenueCat Dashboard](https://app.revenuecat.com) → Your Project → **Apps**
2. You should have a **Google Play Store** app entry. If not, create one:
   - Platform: **Google Play Store**
   - Package Name: `com.my.AJR.android`
3. In the Google Play app settings, you need to provide:
   - **Service Account credentials JSON** (from Google Cloud Console)
   
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Google Cloud Service Account Setup:**
> 1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com) → **IAM & Admin** → **Service Accounts**
> 2. Create a new service account (or use existing one)
> 3. Grant it the role: **Pub/Sub Admin** (for real-time notifications)
> 4. Create a **JSON key** and download it
> 5. Go to [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console) → **Settings** → **API access**
> 6. Link the Google Cloud project
> 7. Grant the service account **"Financial data"** permission (View financial data, orders, and cancellation survey responses) AND **"Manage orders and subscriptions"**
> 8. Upload the JSON key to RevenueCat Dashboard → Google Play App → **Service Account credentials**

> [!WARNING]
> After granting permissions in Play Console, it can take **up to 24-36 hours** for Google to propagate the permissions. RevenueCat won't be able to validate purchases until this propagation is complete.

---

## Issue #2 (CRITICAL): Product ID Mismatch

In your code ([RevenueCatService.js](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/services/RevenueCatService.js#L22-L26)):

```javascript
const PRODUCT_IDS = {
    weekly: 'com.my.ajr.weekly',        // ← lowercase
    yearly: 'com.my.ajr.annually',      // ← lowercase, "annually"
};
```

But your implementation plan says the Apple products were set up as:
- `com.my.AJR.ajrplus.weekly`
- `com.my.AJR.ajrplus.yearly`

**For Android, you need to verify**: What are the **exact product IDs** you created in Google Play Console → Monetization → Subscriptions? They must match **exactly** (case-sensitive) in:
1. Google Play Console subscription configuration
2. RevenueCat Dashboard → Products (with store = Google Play)
3. RevenueCat Dashboard → Offerings → Packages (mapped to the Google Play products)

> [!NOTE]
> The `PRODUCT_IDS` constant in code is **not actually used** for purchasing — RevenueCat uses the offerings/packages you configure in the dashboard. However, the products in the RevenueCat dashboard must exactly match Google Play Console product IDs.

**Action Required:**
- Confirm the exact product IDs in Google Play Console
- Create matching products in RevenueCat with store = **Google Play**  
- Attach those Google Play products to the **same entitlement** (`ajr_plus`)
- Attach those Google Play products to the **same offering** packages (`$rc_weekly`, `$rc_annual`)

---

## Issue #3 (MODERATE): Missing BILLING Permission

Your [AndroidManifest.xml](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml) does **not** include the billing permission:

```xml
<uses-permission android:name="com.android.vending.BILLING" />
```

While `react-native-purchases` typically adds this automatically via its own manifest, it's best practice to declare it explicitly to avoid merge issues. **This alone won't cause your current symptom** (Google Play still charged you), but it could cause issues on some devices.

---

## Issue #4 (MODERATE): Hardcoded Apple-Only Text & Links

Your [SubscriptionScreen.js](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/screens/SubscriptionScreen.js) has iOS-only content shown to Android users:

1. **Line 115**: "Manage Subscription" links to `https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions` — Android users should go to Play Store subscriptions
2. **Line 318**: "Payment will be charged to your Apple ID account..." — Wrong store text for Android

---

## Issue #5 (MODERATE): RedeemCodeScreen Blocks Android

[RedeemCodeScreen.js](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/screens/RedeemCodeScreen.js#L33-L39) shows "Not Available" for non-iOS, and uses `Purchases.presentCodeRedemptionSheet()` which is iOS-only. Android users who navigate here get blocked. Consider either hiding the navigation entry on Android or providing a Google Play promo code alternative.

---

## Issue #6 (MINOR): Debug Logging Disabled

[RevenueCatService.js line 42](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/services/RevenueCatService.js#L42) has `LOG_LEVEL.DEBUG` commented out. **Enable it during testing** to see exactly what RevenueCat is doing:

```javascript
Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.DEBUG); // ENABLE THIS FOR TESTING
```

---

## Code Fixes

### Fix 1: Enable Debug Logging (for testing)

In [RevenueCatService.js](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/services/RevenueCatService.js):

```diff
-            //Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.DEBUG);
-            Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.INFO);
+            Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.DEBUG);
+            //Purchases.setLogLevel(LOG_LEVEL.INFO);
```

### Fix 2: Platform-Aware Subscription Management Link

In [SubscriptionScreen.js](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/src/screens/SubscriptionScreen.js), the "Manage Subscription" button and legal text:

```diff
 // Add Platform import at the top
-import { ... } from 'react-native';
+import { ..., Platform } from 'react-native';

 // Line 115 - Manage Subscription link
-Linking.openURL('https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions');
+Linking.openURL(
+    Platform.OS === 'ios'
+        ? 'https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions'
+        : 'https://play.google.com/store/account/subscriptions'
+);

 // Line 316-318 - Legal text
-'Payment will be charged to your Apple ID account. Subscription automatically renews unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.'
+Platform.OS === 'ios'
+    ? 'Payment will be charged to your Apple ID account. Subscription automatically renews unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.'
+    : 'Payment will be charged to your Google Play account. Subscription automatically renews unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.'
```

### Fix 3: Add BILLING Permission

In [AndroidManifest.xml](file:///Users/ahmed/Desktop/AJR_APP_V2_3/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml):

```diff
 <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>
+<uses-permission android:name="com.android.vending.BILLING"/>
```

---

## ✅ Complete Android Production Checklist

### Google Play Console
- [ ] **Subscription products created** in Play Console → Monetization → Subscriptions
  - [ ] Weekly subscription with correct product ID (note exact ID: _____________)
  - [ ] Yearly subscription with correct product ID (note exact ID: _____________)
  - [ ] Both products have pricing set
  - [ ] Both products have localizations (title + description)
  - [ ] Both products are in **Active** status
- [ ] **App uploaded** to at least Internal Testing track ✅ (you've done this)
- [ ] **Licensing testing** configured: Play Console → Settings → License testing → Add your test email addresses
- [ ] **Test account email** added to the internal testing track testers list

### Google Cloud Console
- [ ] **Service Account created** with JSON key downloaded
- [ ] **Google Cloud project linked** to Play Console (Settings → API access)
- [ ] **Service Account granted** "Financial data" + "Manage orders and subscriptions" permissions in Play Console

### RevenueCat Dashboard
- [ ] **Google Play Store app created** in RevenueCat project
  - [ ] Package name: `com.my.AJR.android`
  - [ ] Service Account credentials JSON uploaded
  - [ ] Credentials validated (green checkmark)
- [ ] **Google Play products created** in Product Catalog
  - [ ] Weekly product (matching Play Console product ID, Store = Google Play)
  - [ ] Yearly product (matching Play Console product ID, Store = Google Play)
- [ ] **Products attached to entitlement** `ajr_plus` (both iOS + Android products)
- [ ] **Products attached to offering packages**
  - [ ] `$rc_weekly` → has both Apple + Google Play weekly products
  - [ ] `$rc_annual` → has both Apple + Google Play yearly products
- [ ] **Offering set as "Current"** (default)
- [ ] **Google Real-Time Developer Notifications (RTDN)** configured:
  - [ ] In RevenueCat → Google Play app → copy the Google Cloud Pub/Sub topic
  - [ ] In Play Console → Monetization Setup → paste the Pub/Sub topic URL
  - [ ] This ensures RevenueCat gets instant updates on subscription status changes

### Code Changes
- [ ] Debug logging enabled during testing
- [ ] `BILLING` permission added to AndroidManifest
- [ ] Platform-aware "Manage Subscription" link
- [ ] Platform-aware legal text (Apple ID → Google Play)
- [ ] `PRODUCT_IDS` constants updated to match actual product IDs (cosmetic, not functional)
- [ ] `RedeemCodeScreen` navigation hidden or adapted for Android

### Before Production Launch
- [ ] Test full purchase flow on Android device with license tester account
- [ ] Verify transaction appears in RevenueCat dashboard
- [ ] Verify `isProUser` becomes `true` after purchase
- [ ] Verify "Restore Purchases" works on Android
- [ ] Test subscription cancellation (via Play Store → Subscriptions)
- [ ] Switch log level back to `LOG_LEVEL.INFO` for production
- [ ] Increment `versionCode` in `app.json` for production build

---

## 🚀 Immediate Recovery: Restore Your Test Purchase

Since money was already deducted, after fixing the RevenueCat configuration:

1. Open the app on your test device
2. Go to the subscription screen
3. Tap **"Restore Purchases"** — this should now work once RevenueCat can talk to Google Play
4. If restore doesn't work, you can also:
   - Cancel the subscription from Google Play Store → Subscriptions
   - Request a refund via Google Play (Order History)
   - Re-subscribe after the fix
